.TH QFW-DIRSVC-START 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-dirsvc-start \- low-level launcher for one DEFw directory process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-dirsvc-start
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-dirsvc-start
starts one DEFw directory process, waits for its listener, and writes PID and
readiness records. It is retained for compatibility and is used by the
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1)
lifecycle engine. Administrators normally use that manager instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --site-config " file"
Use directory defaults from the selected site configuration.
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Use an explicit component run directory.
.TP
.BI --name " name"
Override the DEFw directory name.
.TP
.BI --host " host"
Override the listener host recorded in readiness state.
.TP
.BI --listen-port " port"
Override the control port.
.TP
.BI --telnet-port " port"
Override the diagnostic port. The default is 8091.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Override the startup timeout.
.TP
.BI --pid-file " file"
Write the process identifier to an explicit file.
.TP
.BI --ready-file " file"
Write readiness JSON to an explicit file.
.TP
.B --background
Return after readiness while leaving the process running.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Write representative state without starting a process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
.BR qfw-service-start (1),
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5),
.BR qfw-service-plane (7)
